`GIT_LITERAL_PATHSPECS=0`.\n[x] Invalid patterns `(` and `[a` return an `error`; a pattern valid for `new RegExp` but rejected by `git grep -E` returns an `error` from git's failure.\n[x] No tool on a live or pinned tree serves `.git/config`, `.GIT/config`, `.Git/HEAD`, `gitlink/config`, an untracked `.env`, an ignored `build/out.go`, or an untracked `credentials.json`.\n[x] Every tool result, encoded with `encodeToolResult`, stays within 65536 + 512 bytes for wide, tall, minified, and many-match files and for 400 long paths on live and pinned trees; `wide.txt` with `limit 3` returns `returned_range [1, 1]` and resumes at `offset >= 2`; grep and list mark truncation.\n[x] Aborting the signal kills the child of a streamed `read_file` and of `grep_repo` (injectable spawn).\n[x] `npm run lint`, `npm run typecheck`, and `npm run test:ts` pass, and the Go build and Go tests still pass.\n\n**Where I went beyond or interpreted the spec:**\n- **Extra argument.** `explorationTools(repo, tree, {env})` takes a third argument, the environment git runs with, the same way ticket 11's functions do. The abort signal still comes in with each `run` call.\n- **Abort.** An abort is not something the model caused, so `run` rejects with an `AbortError` instead of returning `{error}`, and the git child is killed.\n- **\"Injectable spawn\".** I read this as a fake `git` placed first on `PATH` in the injected environment, the same approach ticket 11 used. To prove the child is killed rather than drained, the fake runs `yes` endlessly.\n- **Byte counting.** The size caps in `read_file` and `grep_repo` count bytes after invalid UTF-8 is replaced, so the limit holds on what the model actually sees. For valid UTF-8 this matches Go exactly.\n\n**One limit I kept for parity:** `read_file` lists every cut line in its trailer, including cut lines before the requested offset, as the spec and Go do. A window far into a file with many cut lines could therefore push the trailer past the 512-byte allowance. No test covers that case; it's recorded in `.redeye/notes.md`.\n\n**Bug found while testing:** when a git stream is stopped early, the line reader has to be closed before waiting for git to exit. Otherwise the paused output keeps the process from finishing and the call hangs. That's fixed, and I added the rule to `AGENTS.md`.\n\nThe new code is in `src/context/` (`tools.ts`, `read-file.ts`, `list-files.ts`, `grep.ts`, `glob.ts`, `offset-limit.ts`). Tests are in `test/context/tools-*.ts` and are imported from `test/index.ts`."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":208,"cache_read_input_tokens":162441,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":208},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"4cf29458-5122-401c-87fa-1af933ca42a6","uuid":"6c15eedb-5dfe-406e-95a1-3c9cf04950f4","timestamp":"2026-11-18T20:20:57.409Z","request_id":"req_011ChB1o8udc5Lu1vcUqmLKG"}
